You are assisting with business process modelling. A first check could not decide whether the conditions in the list below hold for the business process described below. They are conditions of the rule [SGD-Art14-3]. Look again.

INSTRUCTIONS
- The legal passages below are all the rules found for this process. Use them only to understand what a condition means (for example a definition of a word). Whether a condition holds must still be shown by the process description.
- For each condition, choose its status:
  - "confirmed": the description states that it holds. A statement in legal terms is "confirmed" when the description states the same fact in everyday words.
  - "contradicted": the description states something that makes it false.
  - "not_stated": use this only when no sentence of the description speaks to the statement.
- "confirmed" needs a quote that itself states that fact; a sentence about a different event never confirms it.
- Do not guess facts the description does not state.
- quotes: for "confirmed" or "contradicted", a list of 1 to 3 sentences of the process description that together show it, each copied exactly and word for word. Use more than one sentence only when the fact is stated across several sentences. For "not_stated", use an empty list []. Quotes are checked automatically; a quote that does not appear in the description is ignored, and an item with no such quote counts as "not_stated".
- Give one result for every condition, with its id, and no other results.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE OF EVERYDAY WORDS (made up, from another domain)
Statement: "C1: the vessel has obtained clearance for departure from the port authority"
Description sentence: "The harbour master tells the captain that the ship may leave."
Result: "confirmed", quotes ["The harbour master tells the captain that the ship may leave"] (the same fact in everyday words). The sentence "The crew loads the cargo." speaks about a different event and would not confirm it.

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "ItemCheck": {
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "description": "The id of the item, as given in the list",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "closest_sentence": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "The sentence of the process description that comes closest to the statement, copied word for word, or null if none",
          "title": "Closest Sentence"
        },
        "status": {
          "description": "confirmed, contradicted or not_stated, judged from the description only",
          "enum": [
            "confirmed",
            "not_stated",
            "contradicted"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quotes": {
          "description": "1 to 3 sentences copied word for word from the process description that together show the status; empty list for not_stated",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "maxItems": 3,
          "title": "Quotes",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "closest_sentence",
        "status",
        "quotes"
      ],
      "title": "ItemCheck",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "results": {
      "description": "One result for every item of the list",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/ItemCheck"
      },
      "title": "Results",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "results"
  ],
  "title": "CheckOutputV2",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
The process begins when a customer files a complaint about a product or service.
Customer service logs the complaint and assigns it to the relevant department for investigation.
After reviewing the details, the team determines whether the complaint is valid and whether a refund is justified and notifies the customer with the decision.
If a refund is approved, the financial team processes the reimbursement.
The complaint is marked as resolved once the customer receives the refund or directly after notifying the customer in case the refund was rejected.
After resolving the case, customers can provide feedback on their satisfaction.
Most complaints come from private persons whose kitchen appliance stopped working a few months after purchase. These customers usually ask for the appliance to be fixed or swapped for a new one.

LEGAL PASSAGES
[SGD-Art14-1] Sale of Goods Directive ((EU) 2019/771) - Article 14: Repair or replacement of the goods
1. Repairs or replacements shall be carried out:
(a) free of charge;
(b) within a reasonable period of time from the moment the seller has been informed by the consumer about the lack of conformity; and
(c) without any significant inconvenience to the consumer, taking into account the nature of the goods and the purpose for which the consumer required the goods.

[SGD-Art14-2] Sale of Goods Directive ((EU) 2019/771) - Article 14: Repair or replacement of the goods
2. Where the lack of conformity is to be remedied by repair or replacement of the goods, the consumer shall make the goods available to the seller. The seller shall take back the replaced goods at the seller's expense.

[SGD-Art14-4] Sale of Goods Directive ((EU) 2019/771) - Article 14: Repair or replacement of the goods
4. The consumer shall not be liable to pay for normal use made of the replaced goods during the period prior to their replacement.

CONDITIONS
C1: a repair requires the removal of goods that had been installed in a manner consistent with their nature and purpose before the lack of conformity became apparent
C2: such goods are to be replaced

